$DIR/main.p:30:6: p holds a view of b (&b, line 27), which was emptied by take(&b) at line 28, so p can no longer be used here
    p looks at memory that b owns, without owning it: the view was made by &b at
    line 27. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be used only while
    the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line 28 b was
    emptied by take(&b), so the view may look at memory that was released, or at
    a value that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use p before line 28, or empty b only after the last use of p
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)
